Stackoverflow question:
 Converting a Number to a Tuple and Memory Error<p>So I have to convert a given number n into a set of tuples using the definition of natural numbers. I figured out how to do that however if I input a large number such as 1000 it takes a long time and produces a memory error. How would I make this code run fast and not take too much memory?</p>
<pre><code>output = [(),((),)]
def n_to_tuple(n):
    if n &lt; 0:
        return None
    if n == 0:
        return output[0]
    if n == 1:
        return output[1]
    if n &lt; len(output):
        return output[n]
    while n &gt;= len(output):
        output.append(tuple(output))
    return tuple(output[n])
</code></pre>

